-- Passage rg3-figurative-language-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d860f7a9-40c6-5fd3-9fa1-b6e6bbdc3d95', 'rg3-figurative-language-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Bread Day$q$, $q$Every Saturday, Ama helps Grandpa bake bread. This week, Ama was in charge of the dough.

"Knead it gently," Grandpa said. "Push, fold and turn." Ama pressed the dough with both hands. At first it was sticky and lumpy. After a while, it felt as smooth as a baby's cheek.

Grandpa covered the bowl with a towel. "Now we wait," he said. "The dough needs time to rise." Ama sat by the window and watched the clock. The minutes crawled by.

Finally, Grandpa lifted the towel. The dough had puffed up to twice its size! Ama shaped it into a loaf, and Grandpa slid it into the hot oven.

Soon the whole house smelled wonderful. Ama's little brother Kofi wandered into the kitchen. "I could eat a mountain of bread," Kofi said, rubbing his belly.

When the loaf came out, it was golden brown. Grandpa cut the first slice for Ama. "You did a great job," he said. "You have a baker's hands now." Ama grinned from ear to ear.$q$, 'draft')
