-- Passage rg3-figurative-language-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('25ef50a8-1138-5b7f-8461-d174190f97b9', 'rg3-figurative-language-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$From Empty Lot to Garden$q$, $q$For years, the corner of Elm Street and Pine Street was an empty lot. It was covered in weeds and broken bottles. People walked past it without a second look.

Then a group of neighbors had an idea. What if the lot became a garden? At first, some people doubted that it could work. The soil was hard and rocky. There was no water nearby.

The neighbors did not give up. The owner of a hardware store gave them shovels. A retired teacher showed everyone how to build raised beds. Kids from the nearby school made signs. Little by little, the garden took shape.

The first spring was a test. The tomato plants struggled in the heat. But the gardeners watered them every morning, and by July the vines were heavy with fruit.

Now the garden is the heart of the neighborhood. Families grow beans, peppers and herbs. Neighbors trade recipes and swap seeds. On Saturdays, people bring extra vegetables to share with anyone who needs them.

The empty lot is gone. In its place is a green space that brings people together.$q$, 'draft')
