   $q$"The bug that had been driving them up the wall was finally gone." What is this sentence really saying?$q$, $q$[{"text":"An insect had chased the two friends around.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A mistake in the code had made them very excited.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-feeling"},{"text":"A mistake in the code had made them very frustrated.","is_correct":true},{"text":"An insect had crawled up the classroom wall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A mistake in the code had made them very frustrated.$q$, $q$In coding, a "bug" is a mistake, and the problem in this story was the block that stopped the frog. "Driving them up the wall" means making them very annoyed, not excited, since Zara groaned about it.$q$, 'draft', 'dac957a5-dff8-5d38-a8c1-2ba349dfc8be')
